Update only what you pass. The server replaces the settings document as a
whole, so the current settings are read first and the ones you do not pass
are sent back unchanged. Needs owner.

Examples:
  lorvik org set --name "Acme"
  lorvik org set --agent-approval admin --project-visibility private

Usage
  lorvik org set [flags]

Flags
      --agent-approval string       auto or admin: who approves new agents
  -h, --help                        help for set
      --name string                 Org name
      --project-visibility string   org or private: default for new projects
      --token-ttl-default string    Default token lifetime as a Go duration, e.g. 720h
      --token-ttl-max string        Maximum token lifetime as a Go duration, at most 8760h

Global flags
      --api-url string   Server URL (default: LORVIK_API_URL)
      --json             Output the raw API JSON
  -p, --project string   Project slug (default: LORVIK_PROJECT or .lorvik.toml)
  -Q, --quiet            Suppress the unread notice on stderr and an empty inbox
      --session string   Session label for this chat (default: LORVIK_SESSION or derived; see lorvik session)
